IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-time-limit`

-- bgg4-tests-time-limit: tests for Art 100 and 101.  Expected values are written from the text
-- before the run: a period of N days after a notification on day D ends on D + N (the day after
-- the notification is day 1: fork F9), and an appeal filed on the last day is in time.
-- Days of the calendar: March has 31 days, April 30, June 30, 2028 is a leap year.

§ `Names for the kinds of decision used below`

`K2a` MEANS `(2)(a) decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement and bankruptcy matters`
`K2b` MEANS `(2)(b) decision in international legal assistance in criminal matters or international administrative assistance in tax matters`
`K2c` MEANS `(2)(c) decision on the return of a child under the two conventions named`
`K2d` MEANS `(2)(d) decision of the Federal Patent Court on the grant of a licence under Art 40d of the Patent Act`
`K3b` MEANS `(3)(b) decision of a cantonal government on an appeal against a federal vote`
`K4` MEANS `(4) decision of a cantonal government on an appeal against a National Council election`
`Knone` MEANS `a decision of none of these kinds`

§ `Art 100(1) to (4): the periods`

-- (1) "innert 30 Tagen"
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the general period in days` EQUALS 30
-- (2) "Die Beschwerdefrist beträgt zehn Tage: a. ... b. ... c. ... d. ..."
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(a) the period in days is ten for the decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement and bankruptcy matters` K2a EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(a) the period in days is ten for the decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement and bankruptcy matters` K2b EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(b) the period in days is ten for the decision in international legal assistance in criminal matters or international administrative assistance in tax matters` K2b EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(b) the period in days is ten for the decision in international legal assistance in criminal matters or international administrative assistance in tax matters` Knone EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(c) the period in days is ten for the decision on the return of a child` K2c EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(c) the period in days is ten for the decision on the return of a child` K2d EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(d) the period in days is ten for the decision of the Federal Patent Court on a licence` K2d EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2)(d) the period in days is ten for the decision of the Federal Patent Court on a licence` K4 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` K2a EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` K2b EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` K2c EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` K2d EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` K3b EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(2) the period in days is ten` Knone EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "Die Beschwerdefrist beträgt fünf Tage: a. bei Entscheiden der kantonalen Aufsichtsbehörden in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen im Rahmen der Wechselbetreibung; b. bei Entscheiden der Kantonsregierungen über Beschwerden gegen eidgenössische Abstimmungen"
#ASSERT `Art 100(3)(a) the period in days is five for the decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in bill-of-exchange enforcement` K2a TRUE EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(3)(a) the period in days is five for the decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in bill-of-exchange enforcement` K2a FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(3)(a) the period in days is five for the decision of a cantonal supervisory authority in bill-of-exchange enforcement` K3b TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(3)(b) the period in days is five for the decision of a cantonal government on an appeal against a federal vote` K3b EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(3)(b) the period in days is five for the decision of a cantonal government on an appeal against a federal vote` K4 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(3) the period in days is five` K2a TRUE EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(3) the period in days is five` K3b FALSE EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(3) the period in days is five` K2a FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(3) the period in days is five` Knone TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "Bei Entscheiden der Kantonsregierungen über Beschwerden gegen die Nationalratswahlen beträgt die Beschwerdefrist drei Tage."
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the period in days is three` K4 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the period in days is three` K3b EQUALS NOTHING
-- the period for a decision: the specific period governs, otherwise 30
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K2b FALSE EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K2a FALSE EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K2a TRUE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K3b FALSE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K4 FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (4) the period in days for the appeal against a decision` K2c TRUE EQUALS 10

§ `Art 100(5) and the start day`

-- "beginnt die Beschwerdefrist spätestens dann zu laufen, wenn in beiden Kantonen Entscheide getroffen worden sind": the later of the two days
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the latest day the period begins to run` TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the latest day the period begins to run` TRUE (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the latest day the period begins to run` FALSE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the period runs from the notification, but not later than the later canton's decision
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) and (5) the day the period starts from` (Date 1 5 2026) TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS (Date 20 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) and (5) the day the period starts from` (Date 5 4 2026) TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS (Date 5 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) and (5) the day the period starts from` (Date 1 5 2026) FALSE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 5 2026)

§ `Art 100(1) to (5): the last day`

-- order: kind, bill-of-exchange, notified, intercantonal, first canton day, second canton day, days left out
-- 30 days: notified 1 March 2026, the 30th day after is 31 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 31 3 2026)
-- ten, five and three days
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` K2b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 11 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` K3b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` K2a TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` K4 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 4 3 2026)
-- a leap year: notified 1 February 2028, 30 days after is 2 March 2028
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 2 2028) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 2 3 2028)
-- over the year end: notified 15 December 2026, 30 days after is 14 January 2027
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 15 12 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 14 1 2027)
-- 16 days left out of the count by a suspension (an input): the last day moves by 16
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 16 EQUALS (Date 16 4 2026)
-- an intercantonal conflict, the later canton's decision (20 April) before the notification (1 May): 30 days from 20 April
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 20 5 2026)
-- an intercantonal conflict, the notification (5 April) before the later decision (20 April): 30 days from 5 April
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the last day for the appeal against a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 5 4 2026) TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 5 5 2026)

§ `Art 100(1) to (5): in time, the day before, the day of and the day after the last day`

-- order: kind, bill, notified, intercantonal, first, second, days left out, day filed
-- 30 days, notified 1 March 2026, last day 31 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ten days, last day 11 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K2b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K2b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K2b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 12 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- five days, last day 6 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K3b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K3b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 6 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K3b FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 7 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- three days, last day 4 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K4 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K4 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 4 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K4 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- bill-of-exchange enforcement: five days, not ten
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K2a TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 7 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` K2a FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 7 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the days left out of the count by a suspension move the last day
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 16 (Date 16 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 16 (Date 17 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- filed before the notification: the text is silent (not covered)
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the day the appeal is filed equal to the notification day is not before the period begins
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) to (5) the appeal against a decision is in time` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 0 (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Art 100(7): refusal or delay`

-- "Gegen das unrechtmässige Verweigern oder Verzögern eines Entscheids kann jederzeit Beschwerde geführt werden."
#ASSERT `Art 100(7) the appeal can be brought at any time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(7) the appeal can be brought at any time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 101: the last day and in time`

-- "innert 30 Tagen nach der nach dem kantonalen Recht massgebenden Veröffentlichung des Erlasses": published 1 June 2026, 30th day after is 1 July 2026
#ASSERT `Art 101 the last day for the appeal against an enactment` (Date 1 6 2026) 0 EQUALS (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 101 the last day for the appeal against an enactment` (Date 1 6 2026) 5 EQUALS (Date 6 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 5 (Date 6 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 5 (Date 7 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101 the appeal against an enactment is in time` (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 31 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 100 and 101 together`

-- order: act, kind, bill, notified, intercantonal, first, second, publication, days left out
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the time limit for filing` `a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 EQUALS `the last day for filing is` (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the time limit for filing` `a decision` K4 FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 EQUALS `the last day for filing is` (Date 4 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the time limit for filing` `a cantonal enactment` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 EQUALS `the last day for filing is` (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the time limit for filing` `an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 EQUALS `the appeal can be brought at any time`
-- order: act, kind, bill, notified, intercantonal, first, second, publication, days left out, day filed
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `a cantonal enactment` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `a cantonal enactment` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 and 101 the appeal is in time` `an unlawful refusal or delay of a decision` Knone FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) 0 (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `The duties as regulative rules: traces (printed, not asserted: the stable binary cannot compare a regulative rule)`

-- Art 100(1), 30 days: filing on day 30 is in time and fulfils the duty
#TRACE `Art 100(1) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 30
-- day 31 is late
#TRACE `Art 100(1) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 31
-- no filing at all: the duty still stands
#TRACE `Art 100(1) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    -- no events
-- Art 100(2), ten days
#TRACE `Art 100(2) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within ten days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 10
#TRACE `Art 100(2) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within ten days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 11
-- Art 100(3), five days
#TRACE `Art 100(3) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within five days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 5
#TRACE `Art 100(3) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within five days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 6
-- Art 100(4), three days
#TRACE `Art 100(4) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within three days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 3
#TRACE `Art 100(4) the appellant's duty to file the appeal within three days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 4
-- Art 101, 30 days from the publication
#TRACE `Art 101 the appellant's duty to file the appeal against an enactment within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 30
#TRACE `Art 101 the appellant's duty to file the appeal against an enactment within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Appellant DOES `file the appeal with the Federal Supreme Court` AT 31
